---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.en.json';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

const areas = site.technologyAreas;
const formats = site.activityFormats;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="ROS Guangzhou is an open technical community for robotics developers: vision, technical focus, who joins and how we meet."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>About ROS Guangzhou</h1>
    <p>An open technical community for robotics developers.</p>
  </div>

  <p>
    ROS Guangzhou is an open technical community connecting developers, researchers and founders working on
    <strong>robotics, autonomous driving, AI perception and embodied AI</strong> in and around Guangzhou.
  </p>
  <p>
    Built on <strong>ROS / ROS 2</strong> (Robot Operating System), the community runs online discussion and
    offline events to promote knowledge sharing, open-source collaboration and engineering practice — so that
    more robotics developers can build real connections within the same city.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Vision</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.06rem">
      <strong>Connect robotics developers in Guangzhou, and advance technical exchange and innovation.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    ROS has become essential infrastructure for robotics worldwide, yet local developers in many cities remain
    weakly connected. ROS Guangzhou aims to build a <strong>long-term, open, technology-driven</strong> community
    where robotics developers can:
  </p>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li><div class="title">Share experience</div></li>
    <li><div class="title">Exchange technical ideas</div></li>
    <li><div class="title">Showcase projects</div></li>
    <li><div class="title">Find collaboration opportunities</div></li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top:.9rem">Making Guangzhou one of the most active cities for robotics exchange.</p>

  <h2>2. Positioning</h2>
  <p>{site.positioning}</p>
  <p class="muted">Topics we cover:</p>
  <div class="grid">
    {
      areas.map((area) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{area.title}</h3>
          <div class="tags" style="margin-top:.5rem">
            {area.items.map((it) => (
              <span class="tag">{it}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2>3. Who joins</h2>
  <p>The community is open to anyone interested in robotics technology, including:</p>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    {site.memberProfiles.map((p) => (<li><div class="title">{p}</div></li>))}
  </ul>
  <p style="margin-top:.9rem">
    Whether you are just getting started or have years of experience, you are welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Activities</h2>
  <p>To support technical exchange, ROS Guangzhou plans several formats:</p>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    {
      formats.map((f) => (
        <li>
          <div class="title">{f.title}</div>
          <div class="desc">{f.desc}</div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h3>Open-source collaboration</h3>
  <p class="muted">We encourage members to contribute to:</p>
  <div class="tags" style="gap:.5rem">
    {site.openSourceFocus.map((f) => <span class="tag">{f}</span>)}
  </div>

  <h2>5. Manifesto</h2>
  <p>
    "{site.manifesto.belief}" — this is the community's basic premise and the starting point for how we organize.
    We encourage <strong>openness, practice, open-source spirit and long-term commitment</strong>.
  </p>
  <p><a href={url('/en/manifesto')}>Read the full manifesto →</a></p>

  <h2>Identity and trademark</h2>
  <div class="notice">
    ROS Guangzhou is an independent local community organization, <strong>not affiliated with
    Open Robotics / OSRF</strong>, and does not represent their official positions. "ROS" is a registered
    trademark of Open Robotics. This community uses the name in the sense of a local technical community only,
    does not use official logos or their variants, and does not claim any "official" or "regional office" status.
  </div>

  <h2>Content source</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:.92rem">
    This page is translated and adapted from the community introduction
    <a href={site.source.url} lang="zh-CN">{site.source.title}</a>
    ({site.source.channel}, retrieved {site.source.retrieved}).
    Where the Chinese original and this English edition differ, the Chinese original prevails.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    See <a href={url('/en/join')}>Join</a> for community channels. Proposals on collaboration, venue or
    speaking are welcome through the channels listed there.
  </p>
</Base>
